{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: Hugh accepts ChatGPT, Claude, and Goose as sufficient primary desktop host coverage, and also requires Google Gemini consumer. Ensure dap MCP can connect and authenticate in all four environments. Gemini Enterprise does not substitute for consumer Gemini.\n\nCurrent task: validate dap's MCP implementation against each host's published requirements. Recheck primary documentation rather than treating the earlier host inventory as a compatibility certification. Inspect the dap implementation and cite the exact commit. Cover supported MCP protocol versions and negotiation; transport, endpoint, HTTP and session requirements; MCP Apps/SEP-1865 versions, capabilities, resource metadata and MIME types, bridge behavior, CSP, and text fallback; authentication and authorization protocols, discovery metadata, client registration options (including CIMD, DCR, or pre-registration where applicable), redirect URIs, PKCE, scopes, token audience and lifecycle, and host-specific connection or registration prerequisites. Distinguish required from optional behavior and implementation gaps from platform rollout restrictions. Preserve dap's authorization semantics.\n\nDeliver a host-by-host matrix of requirements, dated source links, implementation evidence and checks, pass/gap/unknown findings, and concrete remediation tasks needed for compatibility. Do not infer authenticated connectivity merely from MCP Apps rendering, or rendering from ordinary MCP connectivity.\n\nRecord a separate follow-up for later: perform each host's actual configuration and registration steps, connect to a live dap service, and validate end-to-end authentication, authorization, tool calls, and MCP Apps UI where available. Retain host/build versions and observed results. Keep this follow-up deferred and UNSCHEDULED. Do not assign it for execution, create a timer, configure accounts, register apps, deploy, or run live-service checks now. Hugh will activate it separately.\n\nStarting sources: reports/MCP Apps host support.md and research_notes/MCP Apps host support/ in /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom. Google's consumer setup guide: https://developers.google.com/connected-apps/gpc/perform-the-steps . Read its linked prerequisites, protocol/auth specifications, and troubleshooting requirements as part of the audit. The guide currently labels MCP Apps UI beta and allows ignored UI resources; report that limitation separately from connection/auth compatibility.","body":{"conditions":"Arrange a requirements audit for dap MCP against current published requirements for ChatGPT, Claude, Goose Desktop, and Google Gemini consumer. Produce a cited host-by-host compatibility matrix tied to the inspected dap commit, with gaps, evidence, and proposed remediation tasks. Record a separate deferred follow-up for actual host configuration and live-service validation. Do not schedule, dispatch, or execute that follow-up until Hugh explicitly activates it.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}